            <div xml:id="d1430">

                <pb facs="1147" n="1137" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1137"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/8–349: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Tsingtao</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hawthorne</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-08-12T18:00:00-04:00">August 12, 1949—6
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>235. Reurtel 394, Aug 3. Dept has well to fore difficult position ur office and
                    is giving entire question continuing consideration.</p>
                <p>Pls inform what travel facilities, rail or ship, wld likely be available for
                    withdrawal Amers generally from ur district, for our reference in case decision
                    later made to close Consulate. Also report situation re exit permits.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
